---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@components/container.astro";
import Sectionhead from "@components/sectionhead.astro";

const lastUpdated = "25 September 2026";
---

<Layout title="Privacy">
  <Container>
    <Sectionhead>
      <Fragment slot="title">Privacy</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="desc">Privacy Policy</Fragment>
    </Sectionhead>
    
    <!-- Language Navigation -->
    <nav class="flex justify-center gap-4 mt-8" role="navigation" aria-label="Language selection">
      <span class="text-sm text-gray" title="Current language: ENG" aria-current="page">ENG</span>
      <a href="/de/privacy" class="text-sm text-gray underline hover:text-gray-light transition-colors" title="Switch to German" aria-label="View privacy policy in German">DEU</a>
      <a href="/bs/privacy" class="text-sm text-gray underline hover:text-gray-light transition-colors" title="Switch to Bosnian" aria-label="View privacy policy in Bosnian">BOS</a>
    </nav>
    
    <div class="flex w-full m-0 flex-col justify-evenly px-8">
      <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-3 mx-auto max-w-4xl mt-4">
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          Your privacy is important to us, and we collect as little personal data as possible. You can browse the app 
          without giving us any personal information. We only collect personal data when you submit a reservation request 
          or choose to create an optional account, as explained below.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          To keep the app stable and improve it, we use third-party tools that collect usage and diagnostic data such as 
          screens viewed, button taps, session length, crash reports, device model and operating system version. Some 
          features also check which navigation applications are installed on your device so that we can offer them to you; 
          this check happens on your device and the result is not sent to us.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>We do not sell your personal data, we do not use it for advertising, and we do not carry out automated 
          decision-making or profiling.</strong>
        </p>
        
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-2 text-gray-light">Who We Are</h2>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          Japodium is an independently run app, operated by its owners and based in Bosnia and Herzegovina. The owners of the 
          app are the data controller responsible for the personal data described in this policy. For any privacy question or 
          request — including a request for the controller's full identity and contact details — reach us at 
          <a class="underline" href="mailto:info@japodium.com">info@japodium.com</a>.
        </p>
        
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-2 text-gray-light">Reservation Services</h2>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">What Information We Collect</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          When you use our reservation feature to request guided sport and recreational services (such as rafting tours, 
          guided city tours, quad riding, etc.) from independent local tourist and extreme sport agencies, we collect:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light ml-6 mt-2 list-disc">
          <li>First and last name</li>
          <li>Email address</li>
          <li>Phone number</li>
          <li>Request details: the activity, the provider, your requested date, the number of participants and the indicative price</li>
          <li>If you create an account: the email address and, where provided, the name and profile photo from your Google or Apple account</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          Note that Sign in with Apple does not provide a profile photo, and if you use Apple's "Hide My Email" feature we 
          receive only a relay address rather than your real email address.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">How We Use Your Information</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          We use your personal information only to:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light ml-6 mt-2 list-disc">
          <li>Process your reservation request and send you an email confirming that we received it</li>
          <li>Allow our administrator to review your request and update its status</li>
          <li>Contact you by email, Viber or WhatsApp to agree the details of your request</li>
          <li>Pass your contact details to the third-party service provider so they can arrange the activity with you directly</li>
          <li>Maintain your account and reservation history, if you chose to create an account</li>
          <li>Keep the app secure and diagnose crashes and performance problems</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Reservation Status</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          What you submit in the app is a <strong>reservation request</strong>, not a completed booking. It appears in the 
          app as <strong>"Pending"</strong> until our administrator reviews it and the details are agreed between you and 
          the third-party provider, at which point it appears as <strong>"Confirmed"</strong>. Confirmation means the 
          provider has agreed the details with you; it does not make Japodium a party to the activity itself.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Legal Basis for Processing</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          If you are in the European Economic Area, we rely on the following legal bases under the General Data Protection 
          Regulation (GDPR):
        </p>
        <ul class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light ml-6 mt-2 list-disc">
          <li><strong>Performance of a contract and steps taken before entering into one</strong> (Art. 6(1)(b)) — to handle your reservation request and pass it to the provider. This data is necessary; without it we cannot process a request.</li>
          <li><strong>Consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a)) — for the optional user account and for analytics and crash reporting. You may withdraw your consent at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>Our legitimate interests</strong> (Art. 6(1)(f)) — to keep the service secure and prevent abuse.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          Before you submit a reservation request or update your account information, you must tick a box confirming that 
          you have read this Privacy Policy and our 
          <a class="underline" href="/tos">Terms of Service</a>. That tick records that you have been informed; it is not 
          the legal basis for handling your reservation, which rests on the grounds set out above.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Data Sharing and Third Parties</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>Important:</strong> We act solely as an intermediary booking platform. Your contact details are shared with 
          the independent third-party service provider you choose to book with. Once we pass your details on, that provider 
          becomes an independent controller responsible for your personal data under its own privacy practices. We do not 
          provide any recreational services ourselves.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Service Providers We Use</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          We use the following processors, who handle personal data only on our instructions:
        </p>
        <ul class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light ml-6 mt-2 list-disc">
          <li><strong>Mailgun</strong> (Sinch) — sending transactional emails</li>
          <li><strong>Netlify</strong> — hosting our website and the function that sends reservation emails</li>
          <li><strong>Render</strong> — hosting our content management system (Strapi)</li>
          <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> — analytics, crash reporting and performance monitoring</li>
          <li><strong>Google and Apple</strong> — sign-in, only if you choose to create an account</li>
          <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> (Meta) and <strong>Viber</strong> (Rakuten) — only if we contact you through those apps</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Optional User Accounts</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          You can optionally create a free account by signing in with your existing Google or Apple account. An account is 
          not required to make reservation requests — it simply lets you create and manage your requests more easily.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>What we store:</strong> When you sign in, we create a profile in our content management system (Strapi, 
          hosted on Render) using information from your Google or Apple account, such as your email address and, where 
          available, your profile photo. In the "Account" tab you can add or update your first and last name, phone number, 
          and email address at any time.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>Pre-filled requests:</strong> If you are signed in, your saved contact details are filled in automatically. 
          Since a request cannot be submitted without a full name, email address, and phone number, any missing details you 
          enter in the form are also saved to your account, so you don't have to enter them again.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>Continuing as a guest:</strong> You can always submit a request without an account by choosing "Proceed as 
          guest." In that case we create no account profile and store no database record of you — but see 
          "Data Security and Retention" below, because a copy still exists in the confirmation emails.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>Your reservations:</strong> When you submit a request while signed in, your requests and their details 
          (including your contact information and current status) appear in the "Reservations" tab. You can cancel any 
          upcoming reservation at any time. A record of cancelled reservations remains stored in our database, linked to your 
          account, unless you delete your account.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>Editing or deleting your account:</strong> You can edit your personal data or permanently delete your 
          account at any time in the "Account" tab. You may also request deletion by emailing 
          <a class="underline" href="mailto:info@japodium.com">info@japodium.com</a>.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Data Security and Retention</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>Guest requests:</strong> We do not store your details in our database. However, the request is emailed to 
          you and to our administrator, so a copy exists in our mailbox and, for a short period, in Mailgun's sending logs. 
          We delete administrator mailbox copies after 12 months, or sooner on request.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>Account requests:</strong> If you are signed in, your profile and reservation records are stored in our 
          content management system (Strapi, hosted on Render) until you delete them or your account. Deletion removes the 
          data from the live database immediately; residual copies in encrypted backups are purged within 90 days.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          <strong>Security:</strong> All data is encrypted in transit using TLS, and access to our content management system 
          is restricted to authorised administrators.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Analytics and Crash Reporting</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          We use Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics and Firebase Performance Monitoring. These collect usage and 
          diagnostic data together with identifiers such as an app instance ID, device model, operating system version and 
          IP address, as well as statistics about reservations (date, number of participants, provider name). This data is 
          <strong>pseudonymous rather than fully anonymous</strong> — it is not linked to your name, but it is not completely 
          anonymous either, so we treat it as personal data. You can withdraw your consent to analytics at any time by 
          contacting us at <a class="underline" href="mailto:info@japodium.com">info@japodium.com</a>.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">International Data Transfers</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          Some of our processors are based outside the European Economic Area, mainly in the United States. Where personal 
          data is transferred outside the EEA, we rely on the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses or, where 
          applicable, an adequacy decision such as the EU–US Data Privacy Framework. You can ask us for details of the 
          safeguards that apply.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Your Rights</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          If you are in the European Economic Area, you have the right to request access to your personal data, and to its 
          rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, or portability. You may also object to processing based on our 
          legitimate interests, and withdraw any consent you have given at any time.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          If you have an account, you can exercise most of these rights directly in the "Account" tab, where you can view, 
          correct and permanently delete your data. Otherwise, email us at 
          <a class="underline" href="mailto:info@japodium.com">info@japodium.com</a> and we will respond within one month. 
          If you submitted a request as a guest, we hold no database record, but we can delete the copy held in our mailbox 
          on request.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority. In Bosnia and 
          Herzegovina this is the Personal Data Protection Agency (Agencija za zaštitu ličnih podataka u Bosni i Hercegovini). 
          If you have concerns about how a service provider handles your data after a booking, please contact them directly.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Children</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          The app is rated 4+ and can be downloaded and browsed by anyone. We do not knowingly collect personal data from 
          children, and the app is not directed at them. If you are a minor, a parent or guardian should submit any reservation 
          request on your behalf and agree the arrangements with the service provider. If you believe a child has provided us 
          with personal data, contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Data Breaches</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          If a personal data breach occurs that is likely to result in a risk to your rights and freedoms, we will notify the 
          competent supervisory authority within 72 hours and inform you without undue delay where we are required to do so.
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-xl text-gray-light font-semibold mt-2 mb-1">Changes to This Policy</h3>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light">
          We may update this policy from time to time. The date below shows when it was last changed, and if we make a 
          significant change we will notify you in the app before it takes effect.
        </p>
        
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray-light mt-4">
          If you have any questions or concerns regarding privacy, feel free to contact us via
          <a class="underline" href="mailto:info@japodium.com"
            >info@japodium.com</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p class="text-md lg:text-left leading-relaxed text-slate-500 text-gray mt-6">
          Last updated: {lastUpdated}
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="w-full justify-self-end text-center mt-16 my-4">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="text-center text-sm text-gray underline hover:text-gray-light active:text-gray-light"
          >Homepage</a
        >
        <p class="text-center text-sm text-gray mt-2">
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-center text-sm text-gray underline hover:text-gray-light active:text-gray-light">Privacy</a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-center text-sm text-gray mt-2">
          <a href="/tos" class="text-center text-sm text-gray underline hover:text-gray-light active:text-gray-light">Terms of Service</a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-center text-sm text-gray mt-2">
          Copyright © {new Date().getFullYear()} Japodium. All rights reserved.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
